  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe #commit-a-navigate-event algorithm first [resolves the transition.committed promise](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#commit-a-navigate-event:~:text=If%20navigation%27s%20transition%20is%20not%20null%2C%20then%20resolve%20navigation%27s%20transition%27s%20committed%20promise%20with%20undefined), and then in the following step [resolves the committed promise](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#notify-about-the-committed-to-entry:~:text=Resolve%20apiMethodTracker%27s%20committed%20promise%20with%20nhe%2E) (#url-and-history-update-steps -> #update-the-navigation-api-entries-for-a-same-document-navigation -> #notify-about-the-committed-to-entry).\n\nHowever, [navigate-intercept-precommitHandler-redirect.html](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/a1d41944f46dc2b9d0d62a5d7210dc1b385a40ee/navigation-api/ordering-and-transition/navigate-intercept-precommitHandler-redirect.html#L56-L57) has a different order: First `committed`, then `transition.committed`.\n\nChromium [first resolves committed, then transition.committed](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/navigation_api/navigation_api.cc;l=273-279;drc=c6742c548ec7e9cbf20db834b966bfddc8fac909;bpv=1;bpt=1).\n\ncc @noamr @natechapin @smaug---- ",
